# The windows a click on the HUD opens: "EKF" opens EKF Status and "Vibe" opens Vibration.
#
# HUD.cs keeps a rectangle where it draws each - at the text, 40 wide, twice the font high - and a
# click whose 5x5 box meets one raises ekfclick or vibeclick; FlightData shows the form. EKF
# Status has five bars (each variance times 100) and the flags, every EKF_STATUS_FLAGS bit up to
# EKF_UNINITIALIZED as "name On" or "name Off"; Vibration has the X, Y and Z bars and the three
# clipping counts. Each is a form shown with Show(), so both can be open at once.
# `ExtLibs/Controls/HUD.cs:1199-1231, 3148-3215, GCSViews/FlightData.cs:3293-3323,
# Controls/EKFStatus.cs, Controls/Vibration.cs`
#
# Plays the recorded copter flight, which sends EKF_STATUS_REPORT and VIBRATION, and needs no
# vehicle. Run from the repository root:
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-hudwindows.gui -- file:testdata/mavlink/autotest.tlog

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 6

expect fly.ekf.open false
expect fly.vibration.open false

click hud-ekf
expect fly.ekf.open true
expect fly.ekf.flags ~ attitude O
expect fly.ekf.flags ~ uninitialized O
click fly-ekf-close
expect fly.ekf.open false

click hud-vibe
expect fly.vibration.open true
expect fly.vibration.values ~ ;
click fly-vibration-close
expect fly.vibration.open false

# Both at once, as two forms can be.
click hud-ekf
click hud-vibe
expect fly.ekf.open true
expect fly.vibration.open true
